 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "The ark only as a symbol: a ship plate for «واصنع الفلك» (it leaves before «بأعيننا», Allah's attribute, which is never drawn or glossed) and for «ويصنع الفلك». No flood, water or people drawn. 37:1-9 is not glossed (both tafsirs paraphrase Allah in the first person). An hourglass for «فسوف تعلمون». STAGING v4: c1 (36-37): the revelation to Nuh, Allah speaking to him: Nuh alone (a blue drop labelled Nuh) in the plain town by day, held wide, no gesture, no glow, and the background quiet over the whole chapter. A seal plate for none of your people will believe except those who already have (36:5-12, As-Sa'di: they have hardened), a ship plate for build the ark (37:1-2, gone before the word of His eyes, which is never drawn or marked), a wave plate for they will be drowned (37:10-11): the drowning is never drawn and his people are not on the stage. c2 (38-39): the ark appears beside Nuh on 38:1 as he goes to it (he builds it: shown modestly, the ark only fades in; nobody helps, the sources name no helper). Three chiefs in dark robes walk in on 38:3 (whenever a group of his people's chiefs passed by), the camera on them; they point at the ark on 38:9 (they saw what he made and mocked); Nuh answers on 38:11 and the camera stays wide through all his words (38:11-39:10); an hourglass for you will come to know (39:1-2). Nobody is drowned or hurt; no flood in this video. The cover now shows the chiefs mocking the ark (38:9)."
 },
